{"type":"message","id":"dce6ee24","parentId":"40900fdd","timestamp":"2026-02-17T17:55:46.930Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good, the doc folder is created. Now let me write the beginner-friendly guide with simple analogies, emojis, and easy-to-understand explanations.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_7f1fc915aec94cea9bdd1c31","name":"write","arguments":{"content":"# 🤖 OpenClaw for Beginners: Your Robot Assistant Explained!\n\n## Hi There! 👋\n\nImagine you have a **super-smart robot friend** that can help you with all kinds of tasks — checking the weather, searching the internet, sending messages, and even doing research for your school projects!\n\n**OpenClaw is like the \"brain\" that makes that robot friend work.** 🧠\n\nThis guide will explain how OpenClaw works in simple words, with fun examples and easy drawings. Let's go!\n\n---\n\n## Part 1: What is OpenClaw? 🤔\n\n### The Magic Box Analogy 🎁\n\nThink of OpenClaw as a **magic toy box** filled with different toys:\n\n- 📱 **A telephone** (to talk to people on WhatsApp, Telegram, etc.)\n- 🖥️ **A computer screen** (to browse websites)\n- 📝 **A notebook** (to remember things)\n- 🔧 **A toolbox** (with special tools inside)\n- 👾 **Robot workers** (to do tasks for you)\n\nWhen you open the box and tell it what you want, all these toys work together to help you! ✨\n\n### What Can It Do? 🌟\n\nOpenClaw can:\n- Talk to your friends on WhatsApp or Telegram 💬\n- Search the internet for answers 🔍\n- Open websites and read them 📖\n- Run computer programs 💻\n- Remember your conversations 🧠\n- And much more!\n\n**In one sentence:** OpenClaw is a friendly robot system that helps you automate tasks by understanding what you want and using the right tools to do it. 🤖\n\n---\n\n## Part 2: The Main Parts of OpenClaw 🧩\n\nImagine OpenClaw is like a **busy restaurant** 🍽️. Let's meet the team!\n\n### 1. The Gateway (The Boss/Manager) 👔\n\n**What it is:** The Gateway is the **main controller** — like the restaurant manager who makes sure everything runs smoothly.\n\n**What it does:**\n- Takes messages from your phone (WhatsApp, Telegram, etc.)\n- Decides which robot worker should handle it\n- Gives tools to the robots when they need them\n- Keeps track of what's happening\n- Makes sure nobody breaks anything\n\n**Simple picture:**\n\n```\n       📱 Your Message\n            ↓\n    ┌───────────────┐\n    │   GATEWAY     │ 👔 (The Manager)\n    │               │\n    │  \"Who should  │\n    │   help with   │\n    │   this?\"      │\n    └───────┬───────┘\n            ↓\n    ┌───────────────┐\n    │    ROBOT      │ 🤖 (The Worker)\n    │    AGENT      │\n    └───────────────┘\n```\n\n**Real example:** When you text \"What's the weather?\" to your WhatsApp, the Gateway receives it and says, \"Hmm, I should send this to my weather robot!\"\n\n---\n\n### 2. Agents (The Robot Workers) 🤖\n\n**What they are:** Agents are the **smart robots** that actually do the thinking and working.\n\n**Types of Agents:**\n\n1. **Main Agent** — The head robot that's always awake and ready to help\n   - Like your best friend who's always there 🫂\n   - Example name: `pluto:main`\n\n2. **Subagent** — Helper robots that do special jobs\n   - Like calling a pizza place when you want pizza 🍕\n   - Only wake up when needed\n   - Example: `osint:subagent:12345`\n\n**What an Agent does:**\n1. Reads your message\n2. Thinks about what you need\n3. Uses tools (like searching the web)\n4. Creates an answer\n5. Sends it back to you\n\n**Agent in action:**\n\n```\nYou: \"Tell me about dinosaurs 🦕\"\n   ↓\nAgent: \"Hmm, I need to search!\"\n   ↓\nAgent uses web_search tool\n   ↓\nAgent: \"Dinosaurs lived 65 million years ago...\"\n   ↓\nYou get the answer! 🎉\n```\n\n---\n\n### 3. Channels (The Different Phones) 📱\n\n**What they are:** Channels are how OpenClaw **talks to different apps** — like having WhatsApp, Telegram, Discord, and Email all in one place!\n\n**Think of it like this:** 🎮\n\nYou have:\n- A **Nintendo Switch** for playing games\n- A **phone** for calling friends  \n- A **tablet** for watching videos\n- A **computer** for homework\n\nEach one works differently, but you know how to use them all!\n\n**Channels work the same way:**\n- WhatsApp Channel 📱 → talks to WhatsApp\n- Telegram Channel 📱 → talks to Telegram\n- Discord Channel 💬 → talks to Discord\n- Email Channel 📧 → talks to email\n\nEach channel knows the \"secret language\" of that app and translates it for OpenClaw. 🔤\n\n---\n\n### 4. Tools (The Magic Powers) 🔧\n\n**What they are:** Tools are **special powers** that agents can use to do things in the real world.\n\n**Everyday analogy:** You have hands 🤚 to touch things, eyes 👀 to see, and a brain 🧠 to think. OpenClaw robots have tools!\n\n**Common Tools:**\n\n| Tool Name | What it Does | Real World Example |\n|-----------|--------------|-------------------|\n| `browser` 🌐 | Surfs the internet | Looking up your favorite game |\n| `web_search` 🔍 | Searches Google | Finding info for homework |\n| `exec` 💻 | Runs computer programs | Opening a game or app |\n| `read` 📄 | Reads files | Opening a document |\n| `write` ✍️ | Writes files | Saving notes |\n| `nodes` 📹 | Controls cameras/screens | Taking a photo |\n| `message` 💬 | Sends messages | Texting your friend |\n| `tts` 🎤 | Talks out loud | Making a voice message |\n\n**How tools work:**\n\n```\nAgent: \"I need to know about Mars!\"\n   ↓\nAgent uses: web_search(query=\"Mars planet facts\")\n   ↓\nTool goes to the internet 🌐\n   ↓\nTool comes back with: \"Mars is the 4th planet...\"\n   ↓\nAgent reads it and tells you 🚀\n```\n\n---\n\n### 5. Skills (Special Superpowers) 🦸\n\n**What they are:** Skills are **special packages** that give agents extra powers for specific jobs.\n\n**Like learning a special skill in a video game!** 🎮\n\n- **SAG Skill** 🎭 = Makes robot tell stories with funny voices\n- **OSINT Skill** 🕵️ = Makes robot a super detective (finds hidden info)\n- **Code Skill** 💻 = Makes robot a programmer\n- **Research Skill** 📚 = Makes robot a research scientist\n\n**How skills work:**\n1. You \"install\" a skill (like adding a power-up)\n2. The skill adds special tools and smart prompts\n3. Your robot agent can now do that special thing!\n\n**Example:** When you enable the \"osint\" skill, your robot suddenly knows how to search social media, find public records, and track information like a detective! 🔍\n\n---\n\n## Part 3: How They Talk to Each Other 📡\n\nLet's follow a message from start to finish! 🎬\n\n### The Journey of a WhatsApp Message 📱\n\n**Your mission:** You want to know \"What's 2+2?\"\n\n```\nSTEP 1: You type the message\n┌─────────────────────┐\n│ You: \"What's 2+2?\"  │\n│   (in WhatsApp)     │\n└──────────┬──────────┘\n           │\n           ↓\nSTEP 2: WhatsApp sends it to OpenClaw\n┌─────────────────────────────────┐\n│ WhatsApp talks to Gateway      │\n│ \"Hey! Someone asked: 2+2?\"    │\n└──────────┬────────────────────┘\n           │\n           ↓\nSTEP 3: Gateway decides who helps\n┌─────────────────────────────────┐\n│ Gateway Manager 👔             │\n│ \"I know! I'll send this to    │\n│  the math robot (pluto:main)\" │\n└──────────┬────────────────────┘\n           │\n           ↓\nSTEP 4: The Agent Robot gets it\n┌─────────────────────────────────┐\n│ Agent 🤖 reads: \"What's 2+2?\" │\n│ Agent thinks: \"I can answer   │\n│  this without tools!\"        │\n└──────────┬────────────────────┘\n           │\n           ↓\nSTEP 5: Agent sends back answer\n┌─────────────────────────────────┐\n│ Gateway 👔 receives: \"4\"       │\n│ \"I'll send this back to       │\n│  WhatsApp!\"                   │\n└──────────┬────────────────────┘\n           │\n           ↓\nSTEP 6: WhatsApp shows you the answer!\n┌─────────────────────┐\n│ Your phone shows:   │\n│ \"4\" ✅              │\n└─────────────────────┘\n```\n\n**Total time:** Usually less than 1 second! ⚡\n\n### What If the Robot Needs Help? 🔧\n\nSometimes the agent needs to use tools:\n\n```\nYou: \"What's the weather in Paris?\" 🌤️\n   ↓\nAgent: \"I don't know weather! I need to look it up!\"\n   ↓\nAgent uses: web_search tool 🔍\n   ↓\nTool goes to internet, finds: \"Paris: 18°C, sunny\"\n   ↓\nAgent reads answer and says: \"Paris is 18°C and sunny!\"\n   ↓\nYou get the weather! ☀️\n```\n\n---\n\n## Part 4: Where Are Things Stored? 📁\n\nOpenClaw keeps everything in a special folder called the **workspace**.\n\n### The Magic Filing Cabinet 🗄️\n\nImagine a big filing cabinet with many drawers:\n\n```\nworkspace/\n├── agents/                    🤖 Robot workers folder\n│   ├── pluto/               ← Main robot's stuff\n│   │   ├── MEMORY.md       ← Robot's brain (remembers things)\n│   │   ├── TODAY.md        ← Today's notes\n│   │   └── skills/         ← Special abilities\n│   └── osint:subagent:123/ ← Helper robot's folder\n├── channels/                 📱 Phone apps folder\n│   ├── whatsapp/           ← WhatsApp settings\n│   ├── telegram/           ← Telegram settings\n│   └── discord/            ← Discord settings\n├── skills/                  🦸 Superpowers folder\n│   ├── osint/              ← Detective skill\n│   ├── sag/                ← Storytelling skill\n│   └── code/               ← Programming skill\n├── sessions/                💬 Conversation memory\n│   ├── 2025-02-17/         ← Today's chats\n│   └── 2025-02-16/         ← Yesterday's chats\n└── cache/                   🗑️ Temporary storage\n    ├── browser/            ← Downloaded websites\n    └── web_search/         ← Recent searches\n```\n\n### What Gets Stored Where?\n\n| **Thing** | **Where** | **Example** |\n|-----------|-----------|-------------|\n| Robot's memories | `agents/pluto/MEMORY.md` | \"User likes pizza\" 🍕 |\n| Today's chats | `agents/pluto/TODAY.md` | \"10:30 AM: asked about dogs\" 🐕 |\n| WhatsApp phone number | `channels/whatsapp/config.json` | \"1234567890\" |\n| Detective results | `skills/osint/investigations/` | \"Found 5 social media accounts\" |\n| Downloaded photos | `cache/browser/` | \"cat_picture.jpg\" 🐱 |\n\n**Important rule:** Everything is stored in **plain text files** that you can open and read! No secret locked boxes. 🔓\n\n---\n\n## Part 5: How to Add More Stuff! 🛠️\n\nWant to make OpenClaw do new things? You can! Here's how:\n\n### Adding a New Channel (New Phone App) 📱\n\n**Scenario:** You want OpenClaw to work with \"MyChatApp\"\n\n1. **Create a folder:** `channels/mychatapp/`\n2. **Write the translator:** A program that knows MyChatApp's language\n3. **Add your login info:** API keys and passwords\n4. **Tell Gateway:** \"Hey, I have a new channel!\"\n5. **Test it:** Send a message from MyChatApp\n\n**It's like:** Teaching OpenClaw to speak a new language! 🗣️\n\n### Adding a New Tool (New Power) 🔧\n\n**Scenario:** You want OpenClaw to be able to play music 🎵\n\n1. **Create tool file:** `tools/music_player.py`\n2. **Write instructions:**\n   - Name: \"play_music\"\n   - What it needs: song name\n   - What it does: plays the song\n3. **Register it:** Tell Gateway \"I have a new tool!\"\n4. **Test it:** Ask agent to play music\n\n**Example tool code (simplified):**\n\n```python\nclass PlayMusicTool:\n    name = \"play_music\"\n    description = \"Plays a song\"\n    \n    async def run(self, song_name):\n        # Find and play the song\n        return f\"Playing: {song_name} 🎵\"\n```\n\n### Adding a New Skill (New Superpower) 🦸\n\n**Scenario:** You want a \"Homework Helper\" skill 📚\n\n1. **Make folder:** `skills/homework/`\n2. **Create `skill.json`:**\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"homework_helper\",\n  \"tools\": [\"web_search\", \"read\"],\n  \"prompt\": \"You are a friendly homework helper...\"\n}\n```\n3. **Enable it:** Tell OpenClaw to use this skill\n4. **Test:** Ask about math problems!\n\n---\n\n## Part 6: Simple Diagrams with ASCII Art 🎨\n\n### The Whole System Overview\n\n```\n                    📱📱📱 Your Messages 📱📱📱\n                         from anywhere\n                              ↓\n                ┌─────────────────────────┐\n                │      GATEWAY 👔         │\n                │  (The Big Boss)        │\n                │                         │\n                │  Routes messages to →   │\n                │  Gives tools to →       │\n                │  Keeps track of →       │\n                └──────────┬──────────────┘\n                           ↓\n        ┌──────────────────┼──────────────────┐\n        ↓                  ↓                  ↓\n┌──────────────┐  ┌──────────────┐  ┌──────────────┐\n│  AGENT 1 🤖  │  │  AGENT 2 🤖  │  │  AGENT 3 🤖  │\n│ (Main Robot) │  │(Helper Robot)│  │(Expert Robot)│\n└──────┬───────┘  └──────┬───────┘  └──────┬───────┘\n       │                 │                 │\n       └─────────────────┼─────────────────┘\n                           ↓\n                ┌─────────────────────┐\n                │     TOOLS 🔧        │\n                │  (Powers to use)    │\n                │ • web_search       │\n                │ • browser 🌐       │\n                │ • exec 💻          │\n                │ • ...and more!     │\n                └─────────────────────┘\n                           ↓\n                ┌─────────────────────┐\n                │   REAL WORLD 🌍     │\n                │  Internet, files,   │\n                │  programs, devices  │\n                └─────────────────────┘\n```\n\n### Message Flow Chart\n\n```\n┌─────────────┐\n│ 📱 WhatsApp │ Your message arrives!\n└──────┬──────┘\n       │\n       ↓\n┌────────────────────┐\n│ GATEWAY 👔         │ \"Where should I send this?\"\n│                    │ Checks: Who sent it?\n└──────┬─────────────┘       What was said?\n       │                     Is it special?\n       ↓\n┌────────────────────┐\n│ AGENT 🤖           │ \"Oh! They want to know\n│                    │  about space! I need to\n│                    │  use my web_search tool!\"\n└──────┬─────────────┘\n       │\n       ↓\n┌────────────────────┐     ┌──────────────┐\n│ TOOL: web_search   │────▶│   Internet   │\n│       🔍           │     │     🌐       │\n└────────────────────┘     └──────────────┘\n       │                           │\n       │                    \"Here's info!\"\n       ↓                           ↓\n       └───────────────────────────┘\n                   │\n                   ↓\n┌────────────────────┐\n│ AGENT 🤖           │ \"Mars is the 4th planet...\"\n│ reads & thinks    │\n└──────┬─────────────┘\n       │\n       ↓\n┌────────────────────┐\n│ GATEWAY 👔         │ \"I'll send this back\n│                    │  to WhatsApp!\"\n└──────┬─────────────┘\n       │\n       ↓\n┌─────────────┐\n│ 📱 WhatsApp │ Your answer arrives!\n└─────────────┘\n```\n\n### Workspace Structure (The Filing Cabinet)\n\n```\n        📁 workspace/\n        (The Big Filing Cabinet)\n                │\n    ┌───────────┼───────────┐\n    ↓           ↓           ↓\n┌───────┐ ┌───────┐ ┌────────┐\n│agents/│ │channels/││skills/ │\n│🤖🤖🤖  │ │📱📱📱  ││🦸🦸🦸  │\n└───┬───┘ └───┬───┘ └───┬────┘\n    │         │         │\n    └─────────┼─────────┘\n              ↓\n       ┌─────────────┐\n       │   files!    │\n       │ 📄📄📄📄📄  │\n       └─────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n## Part 7: Real-Life Examples 🌟\n\n### Example 1: Weather Checker 🌤️\n\n**Goal:** Ask \"What's the weather?\" and get an answer\n\n**How it works:**\n\n1. You type in WhatsApp: \"What's the weather in Tokyo?\"\n2. Gateway sends it to Main Agent\n3. Agent says: \"I need web_search tool!\"\n4. Tool searches: \"weather Tokyo current\"\n5. Tool brings back: \"Tokyo: 15°C, cloudy\"\n6. Agent texts you back the weather! 🌤️\n\n**Skills used:** None (just basic tools)\n\n---\n\n### Example 2: Detective Work 🕵️\n\n**Goal:** Find someone's social media accounts\n\n**How it works:**\n\n1. You say: \"/osint find john smith\"\n2. Gateway knows \"/osint\" means use OSINT skill!\n3. Sends to OSINT Subagent (helper robot)\n4. Subagent uses special detective tools:\n   - Searches social media\n   - Looks up public records\n   - Finds profiles\n5. Comes back with: \"Found 3 Facebook accounts, 2 Twitter accounts\"\n6. Main Agent tells you the results! 🔍\n\n**Skills used:** OSINT (detective superpower)\n\n---\n\n### Example 3: Photo Downloader 📸\n\n**Goal:** Download a cute cat picture from a website\n\n**How it works:**\n\n1. You: \"Get me that cat picture from example.com\"\n2. Agent uses **browser tool** 🌐 to visit site\n3. Browser finds cat picture 🐱 and downloads it\n4. Agent uses **write tool** ✍️ to save it\n5. Agent says: \"Saved as cat.jpg in your pictures folder!\"\n6. Gateway sends you confirmation ✅\n\n**Tools chained together:** browser → write\n\n---\n\n## Part 8: Quick Reference Cheatsheet 📘\n\n| **Part** | **What It Is** | **Simple Name** | **Example** |\n|----------|----------------|-----------------|-------------|\n| Gateway | The manager | Boss | `gateway:main` 👔 |\n| Agent | The smart robot | Worker | `pluto:main` 🤖 |\n| Channel | The phone app | Phone | WhatsApp 📱 |\n| Tool | The power | Ability | web_search 🔍 |\n| Skill | The special package | Power-up | osint 🦸 |\n| Workspace | The storage | Filing cabinet | `workspace/` 🗄️ |\n| Session | One conversation | Chat thread | Session #123 💬 |\n\n---\n\n## Part 9: Tips for Beginners 💡\n\n### Start Small! 🎯\n1. First, get WhatsApp working ✅\n2. Then try a simple search 🔍\n3. Then add a skill 🦸\n4. Keep growing from there!\n\n### Everything is Files! 📁\nIf you want to see what's happening, just look in the workspace folder. Everything is stored as text files you can read!\n\n### Don't Be Afraid to Experiment 🧪\n- Try different channels\n- Test new tools\n- Make mistakes (you can always restart!)\n\n### Ask for Help! 🙋\n- Check the `docs/` folder\n- Look at example folders\n- Join the community Discord\n\n---\n\n## Part 10: You're Ready! 🚀\n\nYou now know:\n\n✅ What OpenClaw is (a robot assistant system)  \n✅ The main parts (Gateway, Agents, Channels, Tools, Skills)  \n✅ How they work together (messages flow through)  \n✅ Where things are stored (workspace folder)  \n✅ How to add new stuff (channels, tools, skills)  \n✅ Simple diagrams (ASCII art)  \n\n**Remember:** OpenClaw is like a team of robot workers 🔧🤖📱 that you control. You tell them what you want, they use their tools to do it, and they bring back the answer!\n\nNow go build something awesome! 🎉\n\n---\n\n## Want to Learn More? 📚\n\n- Read `openclaw-architecture-guide.md` for the detailed version\n- Check the `examples/` folder for ready-to-run projects\n- Run `openclaw --help` to see all commands\n- Visit the wiki for community tips\n\n**Have fun!** 🎈\n","file_path":"D:\\workspace\\appDev\\openclaw\\workspace-osint\\doc\\openclaw-for-beginners.md"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"stepfun/step-3.5-flash:free","usage":{"input":18769,"output":5087,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":23856,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1771350910378}}
